    "rationale": "The orbital soft-tissue swelling, RAPD, and delayed vascular filling on FA indicate compressive optic neuropathy, likely from orbital compartment syndrome, rather than primary retinal vascular occlusion or glaucoma. The elevated CK supports rhabdomyolysis as an underlying cause, but the ocular diagnosis is compressive optic neuropathy.",
